rule plan_choice v1
description "A rule typed with an IME left on for the symbols: the comparison signs, the plus sign, the output marker, the set separators and an ideographic space. The lexer reads each as the ASCII one, and fmt writes it so"

enum region = north | south | east | west
enum plan = first_plan | second_plan | combined_plan

inputs
  region : region
  amount : money[USD]  range ≧0USD ≦1000USD
  units　: number  range ＞0 ＜101

outputs
  chosen : plan

derive total : money[USD] = amount ＋ 10USD  range >=10USD <=1010USD

table choice
policy unique
| region      | total     | units | → chosen : plan |
| north・south | ≦100USD   | -     | first_plan      |
| north，south | ＞100USD  | -     | second_plan     |
| east、west  | -         | ≦10   | second_plan     |
| east、west  | -         | ＞10  | combined_plan   |

examples
| region | amount | units | → chosen      |
| north  | 50USD  | 1     | first_plan    |
| east   | 50USD  | 20    | combined_plan |
| south  | 900USD | 1     | second_plan   |
